{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>To the king of Edom</b> – Scripture does not mention his name because there is no need. But it did mention Sihon and Og, kings of the Amorites, by their names, in order to give thanks before Him, blessed be He, that He did with us wondrous things, for they were renowned for might and had a reputation among the nations, as it says: \"To Him who smote great kings, for His kindness endures forever; Sihon king of the Amorites, for His kindness endures forever; and Og king of Bashan, for His kindness endures forever\" (Psalms 136:17–20). And it is the way of Scripture to mention the names of great kings whose lands we inherited, as in the matter it mentioned in Joshua — the five kings of the Amorites: Adoni-zedek king of Jerusalem, and Hoham king of Hebron, and Piram king of Jarmuth, and Japhia king of Lachish, and Debir king of Eglon (Joshua 10:3), and Jobab king of Madon and Jabin king of Hazor (ibid. 11:1), and the rest of the kings it mentioned by number (ibid. 12:9–24), not by name. And Scripture says, \"Edom said to him,\" because all his people agreed with their lord in this refusal."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:07:09.246833028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}